1
00:00:17,223 --> 00:02:04,063
Please contact turkision@gmail.com
for any inquiries

2
00:02:04,063 --> 00:02:08,683
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

3
00:02:51,498 --> 00:02:56,218
If let that rebel escape,
the Emperor will hang us all!

4
00:02:59,539 --> 00:03:02,009
We'll scatter.
Go this way

5
00:03:32,738 --> 00:03:35,548
You're now in my lands.

6
00:03:36,531 --> 00:03:39,831
I'll send your heads to the Emperor.

7
00:04:11,319 --> 00:04:16,879
My Alaca.
We have lots of secrets.

8
00:04:17,896 --> 00:04:20,126
Do you want us to tell one
to Osman Bey?

9
00:04:24,344 --> 00:04:29,904
Karayel! Do you hear what
Alaca and Bala Hatun are saying?

10
00:04:31,030 --> 00:04:34,800
They have secrets.
What could they be?

11
00:04:35,174 --> 00:04:36,344
We say...

12
00:04:37,372 --> 00:04:39,972
We run as fast as...

13
00:04:40,447 --> 00:04:42,447
... our hearts fly with love.

14
00:04:44,973 --> 00:04:47,513
Who loves the most,
runs the fastest.

15
00:04:48,709 --> 00:04:52,709
Karayel!
Did you hear that?

16
00:04:55,449 --> 00:04:57,149
Look what they're saying to us.

17
00:04:58,935 --> 00:05:01,365
But they don't know that for love...

18
00:05:01,569 --> 00:05:05,569
... we'll fly like the wind in
the whole world.

19
00:05:07,779 --> 00:05:10,659
Then show us, Osman Bey.

20
00:05:14,994 --> 00:05:18,614
Karayel...
Come on.

21
00:05:20,758 --> 00:05:23,438
It's time to fly like the wind.

22
00:05:42,029 --> 00:05:43,509
Osman?

23
00:06:58,456 --> 00:06:59,706
Sofia is here!

24
00:07:26,962 --> 00:07:33,612
I'll take a thousand of your lives for
every breath you stole from Master Yannis.

25
00:07:38,384 --> 00:07:40,064
Neither you...

26
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:48,390
... nor those damn Turks will
be able to stop me.

27
00:09:03,728 --> 00:09:07,058
You must be hungry.
You've come from a long trip.

28
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:09,820
I'll fill you up.

29
00:09:26,315 --> 00:09:28,305
How nice of you to come here.

30
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:37,760
Aygül.
Aygül!

31
00:09:38,348 --> 00:09:39,848
Mother, look!

32
00:10:01,942 --> 00:10:05,182
Look, Batur brother is here!
He wants pancakes.

33
00:10:06,604 --> 00:10:08,754
Let's eat together.

34
00:10:25,324 --> 00:10:26,554
My Aygül...

35
00:10:32,613 --> 00:10:35,413
My beautiful daughter...

36
00:10:37,351 --> 00:10:41,031
Your brother Batur won't come.
Don't do this.

37
00:10:42,466 --> 00:10:45,456
Your brother won't come back.
He met his maker.

38
00:10:45,887 --> 00:10:47,697
He's in heaven now.

39
00:10:49,347 --> 00:10:51,597
Look! He's here.

40
00:10:58,138 --> 00:11:01,298
He wants pancakes.
My brother came to me.

41
00:11:11,989 --> 00:11:14,219
Pull yourself together, child.

42
00:11:15,692 --> 00:11:17,462
Your brother is dead.

43
00:11:19,527 --> 00:11:23,717
Let's go to his grave
and pray, my daughter.

44
00:11:25,305 --> 00:11:29,475
Enough! You think he is dead
because you killed him!

45
00:11:30,888 --> 00:11:37,858
I didn't kill my brother!
That's why he ignores you and comes to me!

46
00:11:59,029 --> 00:12:00,219
Brother?

47
00:12:12,058 --> 00:12:13,248
Brother?

48
00:12:20,076 --> 00:12:21,806
My brother is gone.

49
00:12:24,803 --> 00:12:26,023
He's gone.

50
00:12:31,706 --> 00:12:33,046
My Aygül...

51
00:12:33,747 --> 00:12:38,207
... don't do this, my daughter.
Come, my daughter. Come on.

52
00:12:38,714 --> 00:12:40,204
Come on, my daughter.

53
00:12:44,924 --> 00:12:46,074
Come.

54
00:12:47,674 --> 00:12:50,074
My brother is gone because of you!

55
00:12:51,126 --> 00:12:53,096
Because of you!

56
00:12:53,458 --> 00:12:56,338
Because of you!

57
00:12:56,655 --> 00:12:58,655
Because of you!

58
00:12:58,799 --> 00:13:00,579
Because of you!

59
00:13:13,604 --> 00:13:14,934
Look.

60
00:13:16,731 --> 00:13:18,841
They're beating me up, brother.

61
00:13:20,456 --> 00:13:24,806
Look.
Same me from them, Batur brother.

62
00:13:30,230 --> 00:13:31,670
Save me.

63
00:14:30,852 --> 00:14:32,202
Come on.

64
00:14:35,281 --> 00:14:36,451
Help yourself.

65
00:14:40,541 --> 00:14:42,241
You must be thirsty.

66
00:14:43,546 --> 00:14:45,616
We couldn't beat each other, huh?

67
00:14:59,283 --> 00:15:01,493
Don't I know you, Osman?

68
00:15:02,069 --> 00:15:06,179
If you wanted to win, I couldn't catch
you on top of an eagle.

69
00:15:14,438 --> 00:15:17,058
My heart shakes this way
for this first time, Osman.

70
00:15:17,673 --> 00:15:19,063
I'm very happy!

71
00:15:31,606 --> 00:15:37,816
Your heart is strong. Both your faith
and creed are like steel, my Bala.

72
00:15:38,813 --> 00:15:44,293
But happiness is a test
just like pain.

73
00:15:44,982 --> 00:15:47,032
That's why your heart shakes.

74
00:15:47,903 --> 00:15:52,393
We'll get through these tests together.

75
00:15:56,530 --> 00:15:59,590
The banners we put on
the enemy's lands...

76
00:16:00,408 --> 00:16:03,258
... will be carried
father by our children.

77
00:16:17,234 --> 00:16:20,134
I'll be with you
as far as I can go, Osman.

78
00:16:23,987 --> 00:16:26,257
I don't know if I can give you a child.

79
00:16:29,215 --> 00:16:33,655
But the only thing I know is
that I'll sacrifice my life to your cause.

80
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:44,960
My Allah knows the best.

81
00:16:46,424 --> 00:16:48,844
May my Allah keep you with me.

82
00:16:49,453 --> 00:16:51,023
It will happen if we belive it.

83
00:16:52,767 --> 00:16:54,747
I'm not saying that with my mind...

84
00:16:56,212 --> 00:16:57,842
... but with my heart.

85
00:16:58,425 --> 00:17:00,065
We'll have children.

86
00:17:01,377 --> 00:17:03,387
Our lineage will keep going.

87
00:17:03,387 --> 00:17:06,067
Hopefully, Osman.
Hopefully.

88
00:17:08,134 --> 00:17:10,654
May my Allah allow us to be victorious.

89
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:16,180
May Allah allow us to be from
those who always believe...

90
00:17:16,180 --> 00:17:19,110
... do good deeds and warn each
other to be patient and kind.

91
00:17:19,110 --> 00:17:20,140
Amen.

92
00:17:47,919 --> 00:17:52,629
The day will come and children
noises will be all over our tents!

93
00:17:53,809 --> 00:17:59,789
That day, the mighty state of the united
Turkish Tents will be established.

94
00:18:03,341 --> 00:18:06,401
The name of the rule
of justice and freedom...

95
00:18:07,428 --> 00:18:09,858
... will be heard from far away.

96
00:18:18,846 --> 00:18:23,456
With Hatuns raised by Bala Hatun,
and Osman Bey's soldiers...

97
00:18:23,456 --> 00:18:25,902
... we'll fly our banners everywhere!

98
00:18:26,781 --> 00:18:29,221
With Allah's help, we'll
see those days, my Bala.

99
00:18:30,140 --> 00:18:31,740
Hopefully, Osman.

100
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:45,350
Come on!

101
00:18:46,247 --> 00:18:48,467
Why are we staying here like this?

102
00:18:48,467 --> 00:18:51,617
You asked for a race.
Bring it on!

103
00:18:52,813 --> 00:18:55,673
-The first one to arrive at the Tent wins.
-Let's do it!

104
00:19:44,524 --> 00:19:46,414
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

105
00:20:25,669 --> 00:20:28,289
They got married hastily.

106
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:35,820
They've sacrificed lots, and lots,
and lots of animals.

107
00:20:37,304 --> 00:20:39,024
Lots of animals.

108
00:20:40,446 --> 00:20:42,986
They wasted a young bride.

109
00:21:02,173 --> 00:21:05,653
Look! We picked these
flowers with my brother Batur.

110
00:21:12,869 --> 00:21:15,359
I'll put them to our brides head
during the wedding.

111
00:21:20,326 --> 00:21:22,326
Do they look nice on me, father?

112
00:21:27,905 --> 00:21:32,025
What wouldn't look good on an angel,
my daughter?

113
00:21:32,578 --> 00:21:36,578
I'll decorate everywhere with
such flowers once I'm a bride.

114
00:21:40,292 --> 00:21:42,092
We will, my daughter.

115
00:22:16,975 --> 00:22:20,975
My Bey.
What will we do about our daughter?

116
00:22:22,633 --> 00:22:28,253
Shall we find a famous bogyman,
or a talented healer?

117
00:22:29,298 --> 00:22:31,668
We need a remedy.

118
00:22:33,044 --> 00:22:37,304
Gündüz said we should find a good healer.

119
00:22:39,245 --> 00:22:43,015
He is sending criers to every part
of Söğüt.

120
00:22:43,781 --> 00:22:48,121
Inshallah, we'll find
a good doctor, Hatun.

121
00:22:48,834 --> 00:22:50,584
Inshallah, my Bey.

122
00:22:52,310 --> 00:22:53,970
Inshallah.

123
00:22:56,020 --> 00:23:00,730
My Bey...
You haven't eaten anything for days.

124
00:23:01,067 --> 00:23:02,382
I'll bring you food.

125
00:23:04,606 --> 00:23:06,420
I'm in no mood to eat.

126
00:23:08,319 --> 00:23:10,055
You know my daughter's condition...

127
00:23:11,646 --> 00:23:12,992
...and Bahadır...

128
00:23:14,054 --> 00:23:16,786
...is being watched in his own home.

129
00:23:18,752 --> 00:23:20,463
If Hazal Hatun had come here...

130
00:23:22,146 --> 00:23:24,607
...and ask me ''What is my son's
situation?''...

131
00:23:26,035 --> 00:23:27,642
...what could I say to her?

132
00:23:39,990 --> 00:23:41,677
Now...

133
00:23:42,705 --> 00:23:45,177
...is the time you are needed
the most...

134
00:23:48,557 --> 00:23:50,233
...I'll bring it anyways.

135
00:24:34,188 --> 00:24:36,878
- Welcome. Welcome.
- Welcome. Welcome.

136
00:24:39,804 --> 00:24:41,652
Thank you, thank you.

137
00:24:47,868 --> 00:24:50,270
Kayı Tent has grown up a lot since
the last time.

138
00:24:50,678 --> 00:24:53,676
It became the largest one in the area.

139
00:24:53,805 --> 00:24:56,443
After all, it has everything needed.

140
00:24:56,588 --> 00:25:00,036
- Gold and battles.
- Politics, Saltukay.

141
00:25:00,250 --> 00:25:02,800
Science of Politics.

142
00:25:02,855 --> 00:25:05,951
Without it, neither the gold nor
the weapon have any value.

143
00:25:07,108 --> 00:25:10,060
When we enter the Tent,
many will come to my door.

144
00:25:10,424 --> 00:25:13,628
Know that I don't want tactless people
at my door.

145
00:25:14,738 --> 00:25:17,240
As you wish, Hazal Hatun.
Don't worry.

146
00:25:31,920 --> 00:25:33,056
Hazal...

147
00:26:04,706 --> 00:26:07,852
Subutay who brings bad luck
to wherever he goes.

148
00:26:09,895 --> 00:26:12,422
One who doesn't make a hundred
dogs bark after...

149
00:26:13,591 --> 00:26:15,080
...cannot be called a wolf.

150
00:26:16,380 --> 00:26:18,872
Now stop howling with your
foam at your mouth...

151
00:26:19,472 --> 00:26:22,327
...which is filled with decayed
tooth...

152
00:26:23,393 --> 00:26:25,663
...and take me to Balgay.

153
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:50,461
- How did you find our track?
-We fought many battles with Balgay.

154
00:26:51,031 --> 00:26:55,212
I can smell his blood from miles away.

155
00:26:57,736 --> 00:27:02,440
Take me to Balgay. I have
important things to say to him.

156
00:27:02,604 --> 00:27:07,970
I would die here rather than betraying
Balgay, don't you know that?

157
00:27:13,128 --> 00:27:17,199
If you don't take me to Balgay...

158
00:27:17,676 --> 00:27:20,216
...then, you will be betraying him.

159
00:27:21,514 --> 00:27:26,471
And is Balgay the Merciless incapable
of handling my three warriors?

160
00:27:27,879 --> 00:27:32,800
Don't you see it? It's only me and my
three warriors.

161
00:27:50,570 --> 00:27:54,270
When it's time to do your
own job...

162
00:27:54,847 --> 00:28:00,292
...a man wears his boots and
gets on his way.

163
00:28:03,115 --> 00:28:05,133
I wore my boots and came here.

164
00:28:06,352 --> 00:28:10,898
Cerkutay, Balgay will be glad
to see me...

165
00:28:11,831 --> 00:28:15,138
...after all the times I protected
him in battles.

166
00:28:16,887 --> 00:28:20,159
Come on now. Take me to Balgay.

167
00:28:54,130 --> 00:28:55,465
Hazal Hatun...

168
00:30:10,895 --> 00:30:12,475
Dündar Bey.

169
00:30:13,360 --> 00:30:14,944
Welcome, Hatun.

170
00:30:17,471 --> 00:30:18,977
Thank you.

171
00:30:23,176 --> 00:30:25,096
You are spreading joy, Zöhre.

172
00:30:26,177 --> 00:30:27,935
Won't you welcome me?

173
00:30:41,033 --> 00:30:42,561
Welcome.

174
00:30:48,596 --> 00:30:51,548
With your one word,
I came as swift as the wind.

175
00:30:53,801 --> 00:30:56,369
Firstly, my condolences...

176
00:30:57,190 --> 00:30:59,428
...I heard about what happened.

177
00:31:02,633 --> 00:31:04,385
Thank you, Hatun.

178
00:31:05,765 --> 00:31:07,322
Thank you.

179
00:31:44,478 --> 00:31:46,137
Sit.

180
00:32:02,613 --> 00:32:05,667
I sent Saltuk Alp to you.

181
00:32:06,484 --> 00:32:11,075
But if you had told me that you were
close, I would send another Alp to greet you.

182
00:32:12,261 --> 00:32:14,064
It isn't safe, Hatun.

183
00:32:14,697 --> 00:32:17,407
I'm the wife of the most renowned
Bey of Bithynia...

184
00:32:18,170 --> 00:32:22,541
...and sister of strongest Bey of Nikea.

185
00:32:24,261 --> 00:32:26,159
What can happen to us, Dündar Bey?

186
00:32:42,357 --> 00:32:45,919
- Welcome, Hazal Hatun.
- Thank you, Gündüz. May you live long.

187
00:32:59,805 --> 00:33:01,946
- Mother.
- Your mother loves you.

188
00:33:02,103 --> 00:33:04,271
My valiant without fear.

189
00:33:11,492 --> 00:33:14,271
Gündüz! Strong Gündüz.

190
00:33:15,499 --> 00:33:17,479
The position of Bey fits you well.

191
00:33:19,419 --> 00:33:21,196
Thank you, thank you.

192
00:33:22,125 --> 00:33:25,735
My brother, Bey of Çobanoğulları
greets you.

193
00:33:27,621 --> 00:33:30,213
Because that Kayıs are jihadists...

194
00:33:31,244 --> 00:33:35,013
...he sent ulufe(service pay) to help you.

195
00:33:50,154 --> 00:33:53,490
We greet him as well.

196
00:33:55,063 --> 00:33:58,698
But Kayıs don't jihad with ulufe...

197
00:33:59,227 --> 00:34:01,155
...but with faith.

198
00:34:04,547 --> 00:34:09,598
No doubt on that, valiant.
We gave it with nobleness...

199
00:34:10,651 --> 00:34:13,651
...and you refused it with your
blue blood.

200
00:34:14,255 --> 00:34:15,940
As you wish.

201
00:34:20,899 --> 00:34:23,710
- Welcome, Hazal Hatun.
- Thank you, Selcan Hatun.

202
00:34:36,426 --> 00:34:38,466
You are welcome indeed.

203
00:34:42,555 --> 00:34:46,441
But what is the purpose of
your visit?

204
00:34:49,097 --> 00:34:52,171
Did your longing for Dündar Bey
break the ice?

205
00:34:55,915 --> 00:34:59,353
Longing is the friend of those
who love, Selcan Hatun.

206
00:35:01,175 --> 00:35:05,011
Of course, I missed...

207
00:35:05,739 --> 00:35:08,980
...my tent, kins...

208
00:35:10,585 --> 00:35:12,259
...and my husband.

209
00:35:15,503 --> 00:35:20,034
But let's not call it a visitation...

210
00:35:21,068 --> 00:35:24,042
...but residation for a while.

211
00:35:29,130 --> 00:35:30,453
Well, well...

212
00:35:37,231 --> 00:35:38,981
Good.

213
00:36:03,819 --> 00:36:05,471
Thank God.

214
00:36:08,281 --> 00:36:10,339
Jesus Christ saved you.

215
00:36:12,236 --> 00:36:15,404
We heard what happened to Efendi Yannis.
We are deeply sad.

216
00:36:19,122 --> 00:36:21,058
Emperor's soldiers are after me.

217
00:36:22,242 --> 00:36:24,212
They won't stop until they take me.

218
00:36:25,266 --> 00:36:27,668
If you want, we can go to Nikea for
a while.

219
00:36:28,376 --> 00:36:30,836
We still have loyal friends in there.

220
00:36:31,289 --> 00:36:37,073
No, Helen. There are men waiting to take
my life as soon as I leave the castle.

221
00:36:41,012 --> 00:36:42,628
And I can't trust anyone.

222
00:36:47,766 --> 00:36:50,113
Soldiers, to your posts.

223
00:36:55,496 --> 00:36:57,675
I'll take every precaution.

224
00:36:58,325 --> 00:37:02,916
If you wish, we can dig bulwarks
and get to the war position.

225
00:37:03,457 --> 00:37:09,576
You know that won't be enough to
beat the Emperor's army.

226
00:37:13,541 --> 00:37:17,136
But, for salvation...

227
00:37:19,464 --> 00:37:23,072
...we have one chance.
- We'll do anything.

228
00:37:25,561 --> 00:37:29,741
The only power that can protect us from
the Emperor...

229
00:37:30,264 --> 00:37:32,360
...is Kayı Tent.

230
00:37:35,797 --> 00:37:38,936
Salvador, you will go there...

231
00:37:39,360 --> 00:37:42,297
....and tell them that...

232
00:37:42,772 --> 00:37:47,911
...I agree with all the terms they want
to be allies. Even tribute...

233
00:37:51,633 --> 00:37:54,986
Osman Bey will never accept that...

234
00:37:55,920 --> 00:37:59,807
...we have no other chance than
making him accept it.

235
00:38:02,193 --> 00:38:06,073
The fate of my people and my own
is on your hands.

236
00:38:07,033 --> 00:38:10,560
I give you unlimited authorization.

237
00:38:12,124 --> 00:38:14,666
Tell Osman that I accept all the terms.

238
00:38:15,762 --> 00:38:17,517
Yes, Princess.

239
00:38:33,445 --> 00:38:38,245
Mashallah. Renown of Kayı Tent
reaches to Nikea.

240
00:38:39,063 --> 00:38:40,818
Especially Osman...

241
00:38:42,281 --> 00:38:44,866
...his battles became songs
for the youth.

242
00:38:46,747 --> 00:38:49,210
I didn't see him. Where is he?

243
00:38:49,777 --> 00:38:52,690
You must've heard it. We'll have
the wedding meeting.

244
00:38:53,310 --> 00:38:56,674
They are on a hurry with Bala Hatun.
He'll be here soon.

245
00:38:57,649 --> 00:39:00,514
Well, this is the order of this world...

246
00:39:01,169 --> 00:39:04,378
...wedding on the one side and
mourning on the other.

247
00:39:05,515 --> 00:39:09,345
One side is birth and the other
side is death.

248
00:39:30,305 --> 00:39:33,091
You said ''Osman'' and now he is coming.

249
00:39:34,527 --> 00:39:38,445
Mashallah. They match each other.

250
00:39:43,020 --> 00:39:44,265
Mashallah.

251
00:40:19,859 --> 00:40:22,020
It has been a while.

252
00:40:22,847 --> 00:40:24,403
Welcome.

253
00:40:26,139 --> 00:40:29,438
I can't see you by the light
of our bride, Osman.

254
00:40:36,225 --> 00:40:37,764
May I?

255
00:40:41,148 --> 00:40:43,811
Mashallah. May Allah protect her from
evil eyes...

256
00:40:44,615 --> 00:40:46,596
...she shines like the sun.

257
00:40:54,207 --> 00:40:55,476
Now...

258
00:40:56,386 --> 00:40:59,767
...you say that, why did this
Hazal Hatun...

259
00:41:00,330 --> 00:41:02,724
...return to the Tent?

260
00:41:04,383 --> 00:41:08,006
After all, this time, which wind
brought her here?

261
00:41:14,256 --> 00:41:18,674
Know that it isn't a wind...

262
00:41:19,839 --> 00:41:21,884
...but a fire.

263
00:41:23,819 --> 00:41:26,243
The fire of a mother in my heart.

264
00:41:33,527 --> 00:41:35,800
You are keeping my Bahadır under
open arrest.

265
00:41:41,340 --> 00:41:44,124
And you forbid him to leave the
Tent.

266
00:41:48,421 --> 00:41:50,146
Then...

267
00:41:52,015 --> 00:41:54,458
...you know what happened, Hazal Hatun.

268
00:41:56,897 --> 00:42:00,522
Messengers at borders are more agile
than your weapon, Bamsı Bey.

269
00:42:01,671 --> 00:42:03,477
Is there anyone who hasn't heard yet?

270
00:42:09,443 --> 00:42:13,381
We all know what this dog Alişar did.
We are informed.

271
00:42:16,699 --> 00:42:21,018
But my brother doesn't want the
blood of a brother...

272
00:42:21,614 --> 00:42:24,420
...to be spilled for the sins of Alişar.

273
00:42:45,679 --> 00:42:47,161
Why did you do that?

274
00:42:48,055 --> 00:42:50,305
It won't be long before Osman hear
I'm here.

275
00:42:51,103 --> 00:42:55,513
And as soon as he hears it, he will come
here with his alps.

276
00:42:56,123 --> 00:42:58,474
Then why did we send word?

277
00:43:04,083 --> 00:43:07,262
Geyhatu's arrival at Söğüt is a
matter of time.

278
00:43:10,312 --> 00:43:14,030
Until he does, we need to gain time.

279
00:43:17,084 --> 00:43:19,015
And the enemy within, Salvador...

280
00:43:19,998 --> 00:43:22,600
...will gain that time.

281
00:43:33,847 --> 00:43:37,400
You brought us joy with your
arrival at Dündar Bey's mournful tent.

282
00:43:42,415 --> 00:43:44,648
But you should know, Hazal Hatun...

283
00:43:45,397 --> 00:43:48,702
This well is too deep. To see the truth...

284
00:43:49,640 --> 00:43:51,368
...you should see its bottom.

285
00:43:57,532 --> 00:43:59,171
Selcan Hatun...

286
00:43:59,569 --> 00:44:01,903
...blue-eyed Selcan Hatun...

287
00:44:02,697 --> 00:44:07,713
...thank Allah, there is no well too deep
for us to not see its bottom.

288
00:44:13,782 --> 00:44:16,566
There is no need to blur the point
with fancy words, aunt.

289
00:44:18,598 --> 00:44:20,780
Bahadır moved against the Laws.

290
00:44:22,811 --> 00:44:25,782
A post holds a tent, a Bey holds
the Tent...

291
00:44:26,726 --> 00:44:28,615
...and justice holds the Law.

292
00:44:31,014 --> 00:44:33,920
My Bahadır had blindness...

293
00:44:35,412 --> 00:44:37,902
...but he isn't a traitor.

294
00:44:38,392 --> 00:44:40,601
That matter is over, aunt.

295
00:44:40,819 --> 00:44:42,939
The decision about him...

296
00:44:43,888 --> 00:44:46,576
...will be made by our Bey when he
returns to the Tent.

297
00:44:48,080 --> 00:44:50,053
Be at ease.

298
00:44:50,342 --> 00:44:53,202
I have no doubt.

299
00:44:54,062 --> 00:44:57,739
But Bahadır's uncles won't accept
any decision...

300
00:44:57,769 --> 00:45:01,784
...the will result in Bahadır's death.

301
00:45:04,006 --> 00:45:05,580
Aunt...

302
00:45:07,381 --> 00:45:10,290
...like you are stuck between
motherhood and the Law...

303
00:45:10,838 --> 00:45:13,631
...don't stick us between our
respect for you...

304
00:45:15,306 --> 00:45:17,706
...and justice.

305
00:45:20,589 --> 00:45:23,396
Çobanoğulları aren't like any other...

306
00:45:23,643 --> 00:45:26,131
...Tents or Beys, my nephew.

307
00:45:27,329 --> 00:45:32,006
If Çobanoğulları decides to intervere...

308
00:45:32,006 --> 00:45:34,888
... the only thing I'm afraid is being
stuck in the middle.

309
00:45:35,803 --> 00:45:38,186
I don't want to offend you or break
your heart...

310
00:45:42,440 --> 00:45:44,720
I know the fire in your heart.

311
00:45:45,272 --> 00:45:48,474
But, you should know...

312
00:45:49,303 --> 00:45:51,273
...squares of Kayı Tent...

313
00:45:52,204 --> 00:45:55,601
...is filled with heads of those
who tried to intervene.

314
00:46:01,222 --> 00:46:03,022
We know you as a traditional person.

315
00:46:03,226 --> 00:46:05,476
We love you because you are
a traditional person.

316
00:46:05,527 --> 00:46:07,467
Don't be overwhelmed by your
feelings...

317
00:46:08,399 --> 00:46:10,979
...so that your don't lose your dignity
against us.

318
00:46:20,111 --> 00:46:22,321
Now, it's not the time to talk
these.

319
00:46:23,754 --> 00:46:25,064
I have feast this evening.

320
00:46:26,410 --> 00:46:28,390
You're all invited.

321
00:46:32,121 --> 00:46:33,631
Now, take care.

322
00:46:35,478 --> 00:46:37,508
We need to do preparation
for the feast.

323
00:46:39,044 --> 00:46:41,114
You fulfill your longings.

324
00:46:47,373 --> 00:46:48,173
Come on.

325
00:48:34,353 --> 00:48:36,643
Did Geyhatu send you as ambassador?

326
00:48:36,870 --> 00:48:38,760
Did you think...

327
00:48:40,447 --> 00:48:44,787
...Osman who you trust would save you
from the fury of Geyhatu?

328
00:48:47,720 --> 00:48:50,250
Osman needs me in order to be alive.

329
00:48:50,815 --> 00:48:54,815
Balgay trusts someone else.

330
00:48:57,307 --> 00:48:59,617
Geyhatu knows well what he wants
to do.

331
00:49:00,420 --> 00:49:03,080
He took his precaution and came.

332
00:49:06,737 --> 00:49:08,147
What kind of precaution?

333
00:49:09,313 --> 00:49:11,173
I killed all the soldiers
one by one...

334
00:49:11,739 --> 00:49:16,889
...who would fight with you and
I came here.

335
00:49:30,862 --> 00:49:34,992
Now, you're alone, Balgay.

336
00:49:38,453 --> 00:49:39,873
Shhhh!

337
00:49:43,259 --> 00:49:47,259
You're still precious for Geyhatu,
Balgay.

338
00:49:51,003 --> 00:49:53,803
The problem of Geyhatu is
Osman.

339
00:49:55,349 --> 00:49:56,569
He wants him.

340
00:49:58,536 --> 00:50:04,726
You know well that he will smash all
Kayı's and all Tents belong to them.

341
00:50:05,572 --> 00:50:08,822
Sofia couldn't do the job.

342
00:50:11,764 --> 00:50:18,964
If you give us Osman, by entering into Geyhatu's service
we can have the power to loot the Byzantium.

343
00:50:20,956 --> 00:50:24,306
Did Geyhatu tell you that?

344
00:50:24,898 --> 00:50:28,718
Either me or Geyhatu..

345
00:50:29,438 --> 00:50:30,888
What difference does it make?

346
00:50:31,887 --> 00:50:36,907
Do you think Geyhatu will want what
I don't want?

347
00:50:38,317 --> 00:50:43,997
The grandson of Kulagu, Baytuğ wants
Geyhatu to be killed.

348
00:50:45,359 --> 00:50:48,599
By conquering the Anatolia.

349
00:50:53,703 --> 00:50:54,783
You...

350
00:50:58,596 --> 00:51:04,566
You want to use my power to make
Geyhatu stronger.

351
00:51:05,584 --> 00:51:10,234
You want to be exalted in Geyhatu's mind.

352
00:51:15,566 --> 00:51:16,346
Balgay.

353
00:51:17,173 --> 00:51:18,043
Come.

354
00:51:18,937 --> 00:51:20,857
Come. Let's be strong together.

355
00:51:21,434 --> 00:51:28,974
Let's be stronger and wealthier in the
uplands glorious as Tengri Mountain.

356
00:51:31,853 --> 00:51:35,093
If you enter into Geyhatu's service...

357
00:51:35,873 --> 00:51:37,893
...we'll be the winner.

358
00:51:38,418 --> 00:51:46,648
When you're done, whom of you will behead
me?

359
00:51:50,204 --> 00:51:56,614
I can save you from the fury of Geyhatu.

360
00:51:58,845 --> 00:52:06,375
I can take your old dignity and
wealth back.

361
00:52:07,402 --> 00:52:12,342
Your old soldier, your blood brother,
Subutay!

362
00:53:06,195 --> 00:53:07,555
Princess Sofia.

363
00:53:09,166 --> 00:53:11,966
From the Margaret monks, Alexis.

364
00:53:12,903 --> 00:53:14,823
It's very nice to see you.

365
00:53:15,322 --> 00:53:18,462
We heard about what happened to Mr. Yannis
and other monks.

366
00:53:19,422 --> 00:53:23,422
Our all plans are failed because of a
goatherd named Osman.

367
00:53:25,261 --> 00:53:28,871
We'll take our revenge together, Alexis.

368
00:53:31,753 --> 00:53:38,073
I heard that the daughter of Dündar Bey got
sick and that they're looking for a doctor.

369
00:53:42,270 --> 00:53:46,800
If you ask me to come for this,
you know I'm not a doctor.

370
00:53:51,290 --> 00:53:57,960
I don't need a doctor. I need a magician...

371
00:53:57,995 --> 00:54:01,765
...who can trick them with his plans.

372
00:54:10,187 --> 00:54:15,447
In this pouch, we have the potion of our
revenge.

373
00:54:20,533 --> 00:54:24,533
This potion will make you an
unforgettable hero, Alexis.

374
00:54:44,702 --> 00:54:48,472
Now, listen to what I say carefully,
Alexis.

375
00:54:51,287 --> 00:54:52,337
Uncle.

376
00:54:55,241 --> 00:54:57,091
Zöhre Hatun.

377
00:54:58,191 --> 00:54:59,921
And now, Hazal Hatun.

378
00:55:07,001 --> 00:55:09,241
Hazal is not like Zöhre, my son.

379
00:55:09,563 --> 00:55:12,523
She is powerful and knows
what to do in any condition.

380
00:55:13,436 --> 00:55:15,246
I assume she won't adapt to
Zöhre.

381
00:55:15,335 --> 00:55:16,935
That's the point, mother.

382
00:55:17,565 --> 00:55:20,495
She is both powerful and respectful.

383
00:55:23,312 --> 00:55:26,762
She can do unexpected move in an
unexpected time and you will be surprised.

384
00:55:27,242 --> 00:55:30,352
You be careful, mother.

385
00:55:31,483 --> 00:55:35,633
You know Zöhre Hatun. She's done
something like betrayal.

386
00:55:36,765 --> 00:55:39,335
She never gets well with Hazal Hatun.

387
00:55:40,745 --> 00:55:42,885
Hazal Hatun looks dignified.

388
00:55:43,256 --> 00:55:45,516
Yes, she is.

389
00:55:45,946 --> 00:55:48,106
The essence of man
is inside, my daughter.

390
00:55:48,446 --> 00:55:50,556
Yes, it's inside.

391
00:55:51,009 --> 00:55:53,419
Do you think why she came here
after years?

392
00:55:54,378 --> 00:55:55,978
Just for Bahadır?

393
00:55:57,584 --> 00:55:58,864
I don't think so.

394
00:56:01,107 --> 00:56:04,257
As she is trying to threat us secretly...

395
00:56:05,485 --> 00:56:07,495
...there is absolutely a problem.

396
00:56:08,024 --> 00:56:09,544
You're right, my son.

397
00:56:10,847 --> 00:56:14,467
You don't worry. I'll keep an eye on her.

398
00:56:15,681 --> 00:56:18,251
With the fuss of the feast, we're
absent-minded.

399
00:56:18,390 --> 00:56:20,430
Be careful about Hazal Hatun.

400
00:56:21,744 --> 00:56:23,874
Those like her loves foggy weather.

401
00:56:28,236 --> 00:56:30,026
Keep your eyes open.

402
00:57:44,868 --> 00:57:46,888
What do you want, Zöhre Hatun?

403
00:57:50,593 --> 00:57:52,803
Come and sit down you're standing
on your leg.

404
00:57:52,826 --> 00:57:54,356
I didn't come here to have fun.

405
00:57:55,235 --> 00:57:57,345
I have 2 words to tell you.

406
00:58:08,057 --> 00:58:09,257
I hope nothing is wrong.

407
00:58:09,927 --> 00:58:11,567
What's the reason
for your anger?

408
00:58:19,808 --> 00:58:21,648
You came here for Dündar.

409
00:58:22,122 --> 00:58:24,302
You're saying I'll stay
here for a short time.

410
00:58:24,743 --> 00:58:28,083
But I know. You won't go until you
disturb my peace.

411
00:58:28,348 --> 00:58:30,498
Dündar bey is engaged with me.

412
00:58:31,718 --> 00:58:34,788
If he says don't go, I'll stay surely.

413
00:58:35,899 --> 00:58:41,479
As for you, you'll get used to 3
mattresses in front of the Tent.

414
00:58:41,650 --> 00:58:42,670
What can we do?

415
00:58:43,012 --> 00:58:43,722
You.

416
00:58:44,663 --> 00:58:45,403
Me.

417
00:58:47,482 --> 00:58:48,572
And Dündar Bey.

418
00:58:48,925 --> 00:58:52,185
I've relieved him for years after you.

419
00:58:53,065 --> 00:58:55,585
He has relieved his pain
with my compassion.

420
00:58:55,685 --> 00:58:58,705
I attached his sword to his waist
when he was going to the war.

421
00:58:58,872 --> 00:59:01,122
So, why are you worrying then?

422
00:59:01,428 --> 00:59:05,068
You've always scorned and looked down on
me.

423
00:59:05,648 --> 00:59:06,988
You've looked down upon.

424
00:59:07,554 --> 00:59:09,904
But it's over now.

425
00:59:10,353 --> 00:59:17,353
You, Hazal Hatun, are coming from
a huge and noble Bey family.

426
00:59:17,919 --> 00:59:23,219
I am an orphan from Karabudu, Zöhre.

427
00:59:23,390 --> 00:59:25,150
You remember your place.

428
00:59:25,261 --> 00:59:26,461
It's nice.

429
00:59:26,712 --> 00:59:31,082
Then you must know how to speak
with me, Zöhre Hatun.

430
00:59:32,047 --> 00:59:35,007
Be respectful and be yourself!

431
00:59:35,812 --> 00:59:37,222
You speak right.

432
00:59:37,900 --> 00:59:39,070
I'll remember
my place.

433
00:59:40,056 --> 00:59:42,186
I'll not allow you.

434
00:59:44,120 --> 00:59:47,620
It's not the old Zöhre against you.
You know this as well.

435
00:59:50,227 --> 00:59:52,067
Go and pray.

436
00:59:53,775 --> 00:59:57,745
Pray so that I don't get angry.

437
00:59:58,692 --> 01:00:05,632
Who was the person that made Bahadır
and Dündar Bey offend to each other...

438
01:00:06,476 --> 01:00:10,406
...and made us to leave from here with
my son?

439
01:00:12,518 --> 01:00:15,538
Who was the person that
disturbed my peace?

440
01:00:17,681 --> 01:00:19,121
Look, hatun.

441
01:00:20,620 --> 01:00:24,490
I didn't come here by wishing revenge.

442
01:00:25,513 --> 01:00:27,753
If my aim was to take revenge...

443
01:00:29,446 --> 01:00:35,486
...you would have come back
to the Karabudu already.

444
01:00:36,558 --> 01:00:38,498
My only worry is my son.

445
01:00:40,219 --> 01:00:43,559
Now, go and mind your business!

446
01:00:44,258 --> 01:00:48,258
Don't you ever do anything that will
make me angry!

447
01:00:48,779 --> 01:00:56,239
If you do, you will witness my fury that
you haven't seen till now.

448
01:00:56,424 --> 01:01:02,184
Only Allah knows who will witness
the fury of the other.

449
01:01:03,603 --> 01:01:08,933
Know that Zöhre isn't the old
Zöhre.

450
01:01:25,258 --> 01:01:28,278
Keep your eyes on her.

451
01:01:29,229 --> 01:01:31,559
If she leaves the Tent...

452
01:01:32,049 --> 01:01:38,009
If she meets with someone or speaks,
let me know.

453
01:01:38,452 --> 01:01:40,192
Allright, Hazal Hatun.

454
01:01:59,108 --> 01:02:02,078
The fruit of betrayal is sweet.

455
01:02:02,438 --> 01:02:05,478
But it is also toxic.

456
01:02:06,540 --> 01:02:08,770
Kongar...

457
01:02:08,831 --> 01:02:17,051
Let's start with how you took him from slave
bazaar and made him a senseless slave.

458
01:02:17,763 --> 01:02:23,163
Why do you have a treaty that you had made
a long time ago with...

459
01:02:24,004 --> 01:02:26,174
...a slave merchant?

460
01:02:28,100 --> 01:02:29,790
What kind of power is this?

461
01:02:30,590 --> 01:02:31,620
Cerkutay.

462
01:02:32,320 --> 01:02:35,750
Take soldiers and go with Boran.
Bring the laws to me.

463
01:02:36,490 --> 01:02:40,710
If you let me, I'll take this dog,
commander Balgay.

464
01:02:41,332 --> 01:02:44,932
If they do anything again,
I want to punish them.

465
01:02:52,789 --> 01:02:56,529
Only aim in the war is to win.

466
01:02:57,888 --> 01:03:02,318
It seems I didn't teach it to you well.

467
01:03:05,133 --> 01:03:09,133
There surely will be price for
betrayal of Osman.

468
01:03:10,471 --> 01:03:14,841
Commander Balgay.
Avoid from your poison.

469
01:03:16,225 --> 01:03:18,355
Why were you so late? Where have you been?

470
01:03:18,548 --> 01:03:22,548
After I rescued you, I followed Dündar
in order to ambush him.

471
01:03:22,650 --> 01:03:24,670
But Osman acted before me

472
01:03:25,060 --> 01:03:26,310
So, I came back.

473
01:03:26,758 --> 01:03:30,868
I owe you my life, Kongar.

474
01:03:31,831 --> 01:03:33,781
Wish what you want from me.

475
01:03:35,295 --> 01:03:39,565
Revenge. I wish revenge,
commander Balgay.

476
01:03:40,330 --> 01:03:43,780
I want to come with you to kill all
those who...

477
01:03:43,873 --> 01:03:45,043
...revolt against you.

478
01:04:04,929 --> 01:04:07,059
Betrayal to Balgay.

479
01:04:08,004 --> 01:04:10,144
Betrayal to Osman is the victory.

480
01:04:11,932 --> 01:04:16,192
Betrayal to Balgay is death
with the shame.

481
01:04:35,413 --> 01:04:39,043
Cerkutay. Go up to Osman right now.

482
01:04:40,004 --> 01:04:48,084
Tell him that we have new soldiers and
we are ready to fight with Geyhatu.

483
01:04:50,077 --> 01:04:57,577
When he is cheering up, stab your
sword to his belly.

484
01:05:00,803 --> 01:05:07,373
The poison of betrayal may flow
like a honey from your sword.

485
01:05:11,369 --> 01:05:14,849
Osman will be the best present
for Erlik Han.

486
01:05:17,094 --> 01:05:20,604
Go up to Osman, Cerkutay.

487
01:05:36,060 --> 01:05:36,920
Boran.

488
01:05:37,397 --> 01:05:38,097
Boran.

489
01:05:38,862 --> 01:05:41,932
Tonight, I'll hit my sword in such a power
to the shield that...

490
01:05:43,109 --> 01:05:45,609
...its sound will be heard
from Kesis Mountain.

491
01:05:45,688 --> 01:05:47,078
How magnificent, my brother.

492
01:05:48,183 --> 01:05:50,403
It'll be heard...

493
01:05:51,838 --> 01:05:55,658
But let's look who will be the best
in carrying sheeps.

494
01:05:59,455 --> 01:06:01,285
The answer of your question
is that...

495
01:06:03,334 --> 01:06:07,394
...when there is Konur Alp,
you are the you're the second.

496
01:06:08,672 --> 01:06:10,302
Konur, Konur.

497
01:06:11,468 --> 01:06:13,688
You're flying with your wings.

498
01:06:14,967 --> 01:06:18,767
Don't fly too high.
You'll crash hard later.

499
01:06:21,493 --> 01:06:23,613
You mind your business, Boran.

500
01:06:23,704 --> 01:06:27,624
We'll see now who'll fly and who'll
crash to the ground.

501
01:06:32,574 --> 01:06:36,444
You are witness, brother Dumrul.

502
01:06:36,609 --> 01:06:43,619
If I defeat him, he'll walk around the
Tent with one leg like a gazelle.

503
01:06:43,827 --> 01:06:45,177
Are you a witness?

504
01:06:45,710 --> 01:06:46,940
Yes, brother.

505
01:06:47,250 --> 01:06:48,710
Are you okay with that Konur?

506
01:06:53,889 --> 01:06:55,019
Yes.

507
01:06:55,406 --> 01:06:56,906
But I have a condition.

508
01:06:57,670 --> 01:07:01,670
If you lose, you'll do the same.

509
01:07:03,132 --> 01:07:04,152
That's okay, brother.

510
01:07:04,550 --> 01:07:07,490
Dumrul. Listen what he say carefully...

511
01:07:07,589 --> 01:07:09,349
...so that he don't object to it.

512
01:07:10,309 --> 01:07:11,149
Come on.

513
01:07:13,041 --> 01:07:14,341
Wonderful!

514
01:07:15,482 --> 01:07:17,292
I'm a witness of you too, brother.

515
01:07:20,350 --> 01:07:21,960
He's saying he'll fly, huh!

516
01:07:47,745 --> 01:07:52,675
The wedding feast of Aybars was left half
finished.

517
01:07:56,080 --> 01:08:01,060
But know I can see you're growing
up and get married.

518
01:08:01,477 --> 01:08:04,167
From now on, I won't have sorrow
even if I die, my Osman.

519
01:08:06,248 --> 01:08:10,868
Aybars brother will complete his wedding
in the paradise, Bamsi Bey.

520
01:08:13,688 --> 01:08:18,418
May Allah allow us such a thing.

521
01:08:19,056 --> 01:08:19,916
Amen.

522
01:08:20,100 --> 01:08:21,070
Amen, son.

523
01:08:21,200 --> 01:08:21,940
Amen.

524
01:08:24,744 --> 01:08:30,044
Allah took one of your son
and gave you another son, Bamsi brother.

525
01:08:31,624 --> 01:08:35,414
He is such a boy that he is like a
lion. Praise be!

526
01:08:35,705 --> 01:08:38,005
Thank you, Abdurrahman Gazi.

527
01:08:48,933 --> 01:08:50,133
Welcome, my bey.

528
01:08:56,873 --> 01:08:57,903
Sıddık.

529
01:08:57,943 --> 01:08:59,433
Do you have any wish, my bey?

530
01:08:59,545 --> 01:09:02,409
- Assalamu Alaikum
- Alaikum selam.

531
01:09:02,409 --> 01:09:05,369
- Welcome.
- Thank you.

532
01:09:14,343 --> 01:09:17,283
Thank you, son.

533
01:09:18,132 --> 01:09:20,452
Mashallah.

534
01:09:27,714 --> 01:09:30,874
May you live long, son.

535
01:09:31,730 --> 01:09:34,200
Mashallah.

536
01:09:40,524 --> 01:09:47,754
You must have news to come without
informing us.

537
01:10:00,646 --> 01:10:06,646
Bala, my girl.
You take care of the rest.

538
01:10:08,396 --> 01:10:10,896
With the name of Allah.

539
01:10:11,124 --> 01:10:13,904
With the name of Allah.

540
01:10:19,560 --> 01:10:21,970
Mashallah.

541
01:10:26,826 --> 01:10:30,276
With the name of Allah.

542
01:10:34,796 --> 01:10:35,976
Come on.

543
01:10:45,885 --> 01:10:47,405
Come on.

544
01:10:47,836 --> 01:10:51,143
May Allah always give them
tasteful fruit.

545
01:10:51,143 --> 01:10:52,974
- Amen.
- Amen.

546
01:10:52,974 --> 01:10:54,354
With the name of Allah.

547
01:10:54,393 --> 01:10:57,433
Pour my girl, pour.

548
01:11:02,856 --> 01:11:06,106
Her hands are shaking, Selcan Hatun.

549
01:11:06,885 --> 01:11:10,045
Our bride is very excited.

550
01:11:11,581 --> 01:11:14,756
May Allah let us see those days...

551
01:11:14,756 --> 01:11:17,216
...we will see yours, too.
-Inshallah.

552
01:11:20,179 --> 01:11:22,119
Inshallah.

553
01:11:23,875 --> 01:11:27,735
-Aygül.
-Mother, wait.

554
01:11:32,870 --> 01:11:38,450
Aygül, welcome. Come, see,
they are boiling.

555
01:11:39,161 --> 01:11:42,267
Mix it, my daughter.

556
01:11:42,267 --> 01:11:47,528
In the evening, we will eat, drink and
have fun. You'll be there, too.

557
01:11:47,528 --> 01:11:53,728
In the evening, we will eat, drink
have fun.

558
01:12:05,617 --> 01:12:07,597
I don't know any feast.

559
01:12:10,034 --> 01:12:12,434
I've never seen such a thing.

560
01:12:15,820 --> 01:12:18,220
I haven't smiled.

561
01:12:19,781 --> 01:12:22,541
Allah had seen my grief.

562
01:12:28,792 --> 01:12:32,422
Allah gave me a baby. Look.

563
01:12:35,680 --> 01:12:40,410
So beautiful. So beautiful.

564
01:12:40,903 --> 01:12:43,223
Like you, mashallah.

565
01:12:44,948 --> 01:12:49,868
You will have one, too.
Allah gave me one, he will give you, too.

566
01:12:51,108 --> 01:12:55,248
Babies are beautiful, they are innocent.

567
01:12:56,090 --> 01:12:59,050
You'll see when you are a mother.

568
01:13:02,308 --> 01:13:06,668
Inshallah, Aygül. Inshallah.

569
01:13:07,046 --> 01:13:11,216
Listen, can you pray for me?

570
01:13:11,635 --> 01:13:14,993
Can you say ''Give a baby to Bala Hatun''?

571
01:13:14,993 --> 01:13:18,363
I wiill, I will.

572
01:13:24,426 --> 01:13:26,076
Aygül is alone.

573
01:13:29,803 --> 01:13:33,063
Bala is not.
She has Osman Bey.

574
01:13:36,189 --> 01:13:43,419
Then, take this. I'll pray for you
and you will take care of my baby.

575
01:13:48,619 --> 01:13:54,359
I will, of course, I will. Don't worry.

576
01:13:54,827 --> 01:13:57,087
I'll look after him.

577
01:13:59,240 --> 01:14:03,490
I'll go. I'll pray a lot.

578
01:14:11,885 --> 01:14:16,525
I have much to do. I'll come to
feast at the evening.

579
01:14:26,671 --> 01:14:29,761
You know what we lack, my Allah.

580
01:14:31,296 --> 01:14:32,776
Help us.

581
01:14:38,794 --> 01:14:41,084
Make us full, my Allah.

582
01:14:50,127 --> 01:14:54,787
So, does Sofia want to be our ally now?

583
01:14:54,787 --> 01:15:02,226
It is what she told me, my Bey.
The Emperor hanged the Monks.

584
01:15:02,226 --> 01:15:07,677
Now they are after Sofia.
Alişar bey died and she has nowhere to go.

585
01:15:07,677 --> 01:15:10,707
She knows that I won't stop before killing
her.

586
01:15:12,286 --> 01:15:14,938
There is something behind it.

587
01:15:15,638 --> 01:15:21,444
Osman, there is blood, revenge, and hate.

588
01:15:21,444 --> 01:15:28,294
What alliance? I kill that snake at
first chance.

589
01:15:28,294 --> 01:15:31,344
She only intends to gain time, Bamsı Bey.

590
01:15:32,116 --> 01:15:33,746
To gain time.

591
01:15:36,118 --> 01:15:38,758
Then we will play her game.

592
01:15:42,080 --> 01:15:47,740
Sıddık!
Go and tell her. I accept her requests.

593
01:15:49,368 --> 01:15:51,542
But I have my terms.

594
01:15:51,542 --> 01:15:54,342
She said that she will accept anything.

595
01:15:54,962 --> 01:15:59,492
Now listen to me carefully. I have three
conditions.

596
01:16:01,142 --> 01:16:11,432
First, she will announce everyone that
Kulucahisar Castle is owned by Osman Bey.

597
01:16:15,490 --> 01:16:23,230
Second, she will come here by herself
and surrender to us.

598
01:16:24,435 --> 01:16:29,585
May Allah bless you.
May Allah bless you, Osman.

599
01:16:30,249 --> 01:16:31,832
Mashallah.

600
01:16:32,652 --> 01:16:37,272
You said three conditions, brother.
What is the third one?

601
01:16:37,336 --> 01:16:41,016
Solidarity is for Allah only.

602
01:16:41,675 --> 01:16:44,765
Konur needs a wife.

603
01:16:46,941 --> 01:16:52,331
She will convert to Islam and swear to
be Konur's wife.

604
01:16:54,861 --> 01:17:00,001
Yes, my Bey. I'd like to join the feast,
my Bey.

605
01:17:00,079 --> 01:17:04,959
But the mission calls. If you allow me,
I should return.

606
01:17:05,791 --> 01:17:06,921
Thank you.

607
01:17:14,622 --> 01:17:19,512
If you allow me, tomorrow I'll visit
my brother Aybar's grave.

608
01:17:19,993 --> 01:17:21,173
Father.

609
01:17:24,801 --> 01:17:33,081
I'll tell him to not concern about you.
As soon as the mission ends, I'll be with you.

610
01:17:35,972 --> 01:17:41,970
Just to finish your mission, I will crush
that castle to ground...

611
01:17:41,970 --> 01:17:46,307
...by my bare fist against the stone
walls.

612
01:17:46,307 --> 01:17:51,777
Come on, come on. Be on your way, son.

613
01:18:17,633 --> 01:18:19,243
- My Bey.
- Yes, Saltuk.

614
01:18:19,244 --> 01:18:24,890
Hazal Hatun wishes to see you. She has
some things to say.

615
01:18:24,890 --> 01:18:28,410
She waits you at Kozalak Hill.

616
01:18:42,016 --> 01:18:45,746
My Bey, a healer came for Aygül Hatun.

617
01:18:48,986 --> 01:18:50,766
Let him come.

618
01:18:56,352 --> 01:18:59,002
Dündar Bey awaits you.

619
01:19:06,947 --> 01:19:10,197
- Welcome, Efendi.
- Thank you, my Bey.

620
01:19:11,373 --> 01:19:14,779
Gündüz Bey spread the word.
I came as soon as I heard.

621
01:19:14,779 --> 01:19:20,754
My daughter is sick. Inshallah her health
will first come from Allah and then by you.

622
01:19:20,754 --> 01:19:23,634
Inshallah, my Bey.

623
01:19:24,543 --> 01:19:28,333
See about it. I'll be back.

624
01:19:29,860 --> 01:19:34,840
Do what is necessary.
Help my daughter, Efendi.

625
01:20:01,584 --> 01:20:03,224
Cerkutay.

626
01:20:05,666 --> 01:20:09,276
Balgay has a new order for you.

627
01:20:12,911 --> 01:20:15,571
What is his order, Kongar?

628
01:20:37,561 --> 01:20:42,201
You came to stop me from killing Osman,
didn't you?

629
01:20:47,397 --> 01:20:52,227
After now, Balgay will not turn any Turk
against his own kind.

630
01:20:54,529 --> 01:20:57,709
I will kill him with my own hands.

631
01:21:36,710 --> 01:21:39,760
Wait, Aygül. Wait, my girl.

632
01:21:46,727 --> 01:21:50,367
Follow this with your eyes, my daughter.
Watch it.

633
01:21:53,384 --> 01:21:54,704
Come on.

634
01:22:01,545 --> 01:22:03,425
I fell.

635
01:22:06,125 --> 01:22:10,705
I used to fall a lot. My brother used to
help me get up.

636
01:22:11,479 --> 01:22:15,249
- Where is her brother?
- We lost him.

637
01:22:21,248 --> 01:22:23,128
Alas...

638
01:22:32,509 --> 01:22:35,820
What do you say, physician?
Isn't there any hope?

639
01:22:35,820 --> 01:22:39,706
With Allah, there is always hope, but...

640
01:22:40,016 --> 01:22:41,636
...she is badly shaken.

641
01:22:48,936 --> 01:22:51,905
She will get better, don't worry.

642
01:22:51,905 --> 01:22:58,665
Not only for her, I've brought a medicine
to relieve your heart.

643
01:23:07,220 --> 01:23:09,720
Your daughter's heal is in this bottle.

644
01:23:10,330 --> 01:23:14,326
- I don't ask anything for that.
- May Allah bless you.

645
01:23:14,326 --> 01:23:20,076
But the important matter we need to talk
about is something else.

646
01:23:48,554 --> 01:23:50,904
Kongar...

647
01:24:02,323 --> 01:24:09,063
My business with Osman didn't
come to an end yet, Kongar.

648
01:24:31,228 --> 01:24:35,368
You will be the fruit of treason...

649
01:24:37,018 --> 01:24:39,778
...and I will be the poison.

650
01:24:44,948 --> 01:24:52,338
You aren't strong enough to kill
Osman Bey.

651
01:24:53,650 --> 01:24:55,180
Craven.

652
01:25:00,674 --> 01:25:05,224
We won't kill Osman...

653
01:25:05,502 --> 01:25:08,422
...you will.

654
01:25:49,753 --> 01:25:54,155
Who are you?
Who do you serve?

655
01:25:54,155 --> 01:26:00,130
Who I am is irrelevant.
What's important is your daughter.

656
01:26:00,130 --> 01:26:04,260
And thorns that rise up in spring.

657
01:26:05,379 --> 01:26:08,739
Don't you think it's time to get rid
of the thorns?

658
01:26:21,791 --> 01:26:25,781
I'll regularly prepare your daughter's
medicine.

659
01:26:26,833 --> 01:26:29,403
About who do I serve...

660
01:26:31,095 --> 01:26:35,965
...both the health of your daughter and
the revenge you will take...

661
01:26:37,077 --> 01:26:40,187
...is a gift from Princess Sofia.

662
01:26:43,600 --> 01:26:45,520
Sofia?

663
01:27:00,303 --> 01:27:05,173
Before it is killed, put the powder
in goat's forage.

664
01:27:05,351 --> 01:27:08,884
The poison will penetrate the animal's
blood and meat.

665
01:27:08,884 --> 01:27:14,277
But it won't kill immediately. The ones who
eat its meat will die naturally.

666
01:27:14,277 --> 01:27:18,906
They will sacrifice the goat and you will
sacrifice them.

667
01:27:18,906 --> 01:27:25,506
This night, both your heart will be
cooled and Dündar Bey will get to be the Bey.

668
01:28:05,904 --> 01:28:08,364
Hear my voice!

669
01:28:08,772 --> 01:28:12,982
One holy migration comes from the steppes.

670
01:28:14,409 --> 01:28:18,989
It is hard to carry for a dead.

671
01:28:19,859 --> 01:28:25,769
A soldier goes first,
an old man comes last.

672
01:28:25,823 --> 01:28:31,862
Move aside, a goat comes on shoulders!

673
01:28:31,862 --> 01:28:39,662
Come on, Bamsı Bey! Shoot that arrow
and let us see who is the fastest in the Tent.

674
01:28:40,322 --> 01:28:44,082
Did you hear that, Konur?
My uncle is talking about me.

675
01:28:44,900 --> 01:28:50,820
I heard it. Try not to choke
on the dust while coming after me.

676
01:28:50,825 --> 01:28:52,285
Come on.

677
01:28:52,285 --> 01:28:56,445
Come one, then, valiants!

678
01:29:02,613 --> 01:29:05,523
With the name of Allah.

679
01:29:20,187 --> 01:29:23,868
Come on, heroes! Come on!
With the name of Allah!

680
01:29:23,868 --> 01:29:26,038
Ya Allah!

681
01:29:27,221 --> 01:29:29,791
Mashallah!

682
01:29:33,894 --> 01:29:37,104
Go on, heroes!

683
01:29:38,145 --> 01:29:41,392
- Go on, heroes!
- Come on!

684
01:29:53,515 --> 01:29:55,165
Come on, Osman!

685
01:30:04,831 --> 01:30:06,211
Come on!

686
01:31:11,620 --> 01:31:14,050
Come on, Osman Bey!
Come on!

687
01:31:16,199 --> 01:31:18,169
Come on, Baran Alp!
Come on!

688
01:31:31,799 --> 01:31:34,269
Come on, Osman!
Come on!

689
01:31:45,592 --> 01:31:47,162
Come on, Osman Bey!

690
01:31:57,263 --> 01:31:58,973
Mashallah!

691
01:32:07,459 --> 01:32:09,089
Praise be!

692
01:32:26,583 --> 01:32:30,583
But!
The master of this game...

693
01:32:30,703 --> 01:32:32,503
... is Bamsı Bey!

694
01:32:38,822 --> 01:32:43,112
Valiants! Long ago while
I was still young...

695
01:32:43,563 --> 01:32:47,563
... I could carry two rams
on a single shoulder!

696
01:33:10,202 --> 01:33:12,822
Don't talk large like this again!

697
01:33:14,213 --> 01:33:16,693
Brother?
Ayaz?

698
01:33:28,184 --> 01:33:29,314
My Bey...

699
01:33:44,958 --> 01:33:47,058
Praise be, my Bey.

700
01:33:51,192 --> 01:33:53,832
- May your hands be blessed.
- Amen.

701
01:34:00,891 --> 01:34:02,401
Thank you.

702
01:34:33,943 --> 01:34:35,693
Excuse me, Bey.

703
01:34:36,215 --> 01:34:41,075
They're busy with the meeting
in the Tent. I wanted to meet alone.

704
01:34:41,075 --> 01:34:42,695
That's why I informed you.

705
01:34:42,695 --> 01:34:48,175
Your flaws are fine after all
this longing, Hatun.

706
01:34:50,391 --> 01:34:51,461
Help yourself.

707
01:35:12,653 --> 01:35:14,213
How's Bahadır doing?

708
01:35:14,780 --> 01:35:18,210
My Bahadır is distressed
and thoughtful.

709
01:35:18,942 --> 01:35:22,642
All eyes are on him.
His spirit is uncomfortable.

710
01:35:22,842 --> 01:35:25,522
He's upset about his father the most.

711
01:35:27,732 --> 01:35:32,342
I'm quite good at upsetting
my loved ones.

712
01:35:32,953 --> 01:35:35,113
What happened to you, Dündar Bey?

713
01:35:36,400 --> 01:35:40,400
I thought many mountains would collapse
but my Bey wouldn't. What happened?

714
01:35:40,898 --> 01:35:44,898
Süleyman Şah's son has
lost his way, Hatun.

715
01:35:47,130 --> 01:35:52,980
The mistakes he made in this road
have cost him his children.

716
01:35:56,889 --> 01:36:03,319
Everything that coward Alişar touched
has corroded your heart.

717
01:36:03,518 --> 01:36:09,068
But you must think about your Tent
even if your heart is on fire, Dündar Bey!

718
01:36:10,455 --> 01:36:12,785
You must think about your daughter Aygül!

719
01:36:15,646 --> 01:36:17,026
My Aygül...

720
01:36:20,726 --> 01:36:22,976
Don't do this to yourself, Dündar Bey.

721
01:36:25,634 --> 01:36:27,934
I lost everything I own...

722
01:36:28,791 --> 01:36:31,731
... one by one.

723
01:36:33,032 --> 01:36:36,672
First you,
the Sultan of my heart...

724
01:36:37,900 --> 01:36:39,810
... and then my children.

725
01:36:40,961 --> 01:36:45,371
Doesn't matter if my heart is on
the opposite side of the world...

726
01:36:46,183 --> 01:36:50,333
... my heart is with you.
It's yours.

727
01:36:51,238 --> 01:36:53,638
Don't you know that, Dündar Bey?

728
01:36:54,587 --> 01:36:57,927
You never lost me.

729
01:37:42,907 --> 01:37:45,957
- Did you complete your duty?
- I did, Princess.

730
01:37:45,957 --> 01:37:48,967
I gave the poison for the lamb
to Zöhre Hatun.

731
01:37:50,068 --> 01:37:53,748
What if she gets scared?
What if she refuses to do it?

732
01:37:53,748 --> 01:37:55,178
She'll do it!

733
01:37:55,871 --> 01:37:59,251
She gave everything up so that
her Husband became a Bey.

734
01:38:00,348 --> 01:38:04,878
She'll do it so her husband becomes
the Bey and they don't get exiled.

735
01:38:06,663 --> 01:38:08,703
I don't have a single doubt.

736
01:38:09,941 --> 01:38:16,151
I'll be near the Tent all night so I can
tell you how every one of them died.

737
01:38:16,688 --> 01:38:20,408
I'll never forget what you've done, Aleks.

738
01:38:20,991 --> 01:38:22,651
You'll get your reward.

739
01:38:23,673 --> 01:38:26,413
You're the last thing left
from Master Yannis.

740
01:38:26,675 --> 01:38:29,795
We'll share your pain
and revenge.

741
01:38:41,268 --> 01:38:44,488
I'll take Master Yannis' revenge tonight.

742
01:38:46,412 --> 01:38:47,972
The Kayı Tent...

743
01:38:50,991 --> 01:38:53,861
... will be a huge graveyard.

744
01:38:55,500 --> 01:38:58,230
I'm in a dark place, Hatun.

745
01:38:58,788 --> 01:39:03,788
A deserted, cold,
brutal place.

746
01:39:04,943 --> 01:39:08,943
But you heated my heart like a sun.

747
01:39:11,025 --> 01:39:13,235
I've missed you so much.

748
01:39:14,856 --> 01:39:18,056
Does falling down suit
the mighty Dündar Bey?

749
01:39:18,263 --> 01:39:20,523
Does being dispersed suit him?

750
01:39:21,637 --> 01:39:22,957
Please tell me.

751
01:39:25,529 --> 01:39:28,249
Where's the Bey of
the world I left?

752
01:39:28,864 --> 01:39:32,864
No. this is not my Dündar Bey.

753
01:39:34,155 --> 01:39:39,575
Don't think I removed you
from my heart because...

754
01:39:40,391 --> 01:39:47,291
... you exiled our son, my Bahadır
from the Tent and I followed my son.

755
01:39:48,500 --> 01:39:54,510
The name Dündar is engraved
to my head and my heart.

756
01:39:56,726 --> 01:39:58,266
I've come for my son...

757
01:39:58,910 --> 01:40:02,470
But give the order and I'll stay for you.

758
01:40:02,904 --> 01:40:05,094
Oh, Hazal!

759
01:40:05,531 --> 01:40:10,961
Do I deserve a Hatun with
a mighty heart like you?

760
01:40:13,020 --> 01:40:16,160
You're my man.

761
01:40:19,877 --> 01:40:23,877
It will stay this way until
my last breath.

762
01:40:31,086 --> 01:40:32,936
Bring it, come on.

763
01:40:34,157 --> 01:40:35,367
Let's see.

764
01:40:46,260 --> 01:40:47,730
Wait, make way.

765
01:41:03,570 --> 01:41:04,970
Wonderful!

766
01:41:05,470 --> 01:41:10,240
Good! Mark these.
They're healthy.

767
01:41:12,086 --> 01:41:13,656
Being this one too.

768
01:41:14,052 --> 01:41:16,562
Spare these for the Bey's table, okay?

769
01:41:17,322 --> 01:41:18,632
May it be easy.

770
01:41:43,024 --> 01:41:44,594
Yes, mark them.

771
01:41:45,457 --> 01:41:46,457
Mark them.

772
01:42:18,150 --> 01:42:21,640
They'll kill the goats,
and you'll kill them.

773
01:42:22,146 --> 01:42:24,716
Tonight, your heart will cool down...

774
01:42:24,716 --> 01:42:28,656
... and also Dündar Bey
will take the lead again.

775
01:43:07,404 --> 01:43:08,994
Yes, eat it.

776
01:43:09,784 --> 01:43:11,574
Until you have enough.

777
01:43:12,381 --> 01:43:15,491
So that Osman can have
enough of his death.

778
01:43:17,425 --> 01:43:21,045
Everyone around him...

779
01:43:23,049 --> 01:43:25,289
... everyone who eats from his table...

780
01:43:25,402 --> 01:43:27,542
... shall die one by one.

781
01:43:29,482 --> 01:43:30,382
Eat it.

782
01:44:13,471 --> 01:44:16,971
Praise be!

783
01:44:17,361 --> 01:44:18,889
Prasie be!

784
01:44:19,388 --> 01:44:21,858
People!

785
01:44:23,211 --> 01:44:27,631
We've made a feast!
Many cauldrons are full!

786
01:44:29,837 --> 01:44:36,027
My Osman Bey became a groom,
the fire in his heart has burst!

787
01:44:37,306 --> 01:44:41,586
He came all the way to the bride's house!

788
01:44:42,496 --> 01:44:46,496
Let your bride come and be our crown!

789
01:44:47,850 --> 01:44:52,490
Let her come and honour our Osman Bey!

790
01:44:53,151 --> 01:44:55,331
How wonderful!

791
01:44:56,147 --> 01:44:57,917
Praise be my valiant!

792
01:45:02,636 --> 01:45:04,336
How wonderful!

793
01:45:29,094 --> 01:45:32,894
Your hands shall be dexterous,
you shall make more from less.

794
01:45:42,186 --> 01:45:47,076
May your hands, face, words
be sweet like honey.

795
01:45:54,271 --> 01:45:56,531
You shall always smile at your Bey.

796
01:46:05,319 --> 01:46:08,869
May plentifulness always be in your home.

797
01:46:10,750 --> 01:46:15,080
You shall always be grateful.
In the name of Allah!

798
01:49:11,675 --> 01:49:13,675
What did my Osman Bey do?

799
01:49:13,675 --> 01:49:16,905
He laid the table for a wedding feast!

800
01:49:16,905 --> 01:49:18,205
Come on!

801
01:49:19,254 --> 01:49:21,884
What did he do for Bala Hatun?

802
01:49:22,042 --> 01:49:26,232
He sacrificed many, many animals!

803
01:49:27,071 --> 01:49:28,301
Let's go!

804
01:49:40,000 --> 01:49:43,780
Did he break hearts?
Did he say bad words?

805
01:49:43,780 --> 01:49:46,500
He neither broke hearts
nor said bad words!

806
01:49:47,496 --> 01:49:50,626
He lost his heart to his Hatun!

807
01:49:50,626 --> 01:49:55,236
Then Allah shall make them happy!

808
01:49:55,320 --> 01:49:58,180
- Amen!
- May their marriage last long!

809
01:50:58,792 --> 01:51:00,732
Come on!

810
01:52:36,644 --> 01:52:37,654
Come on.

811
01:53:18,489 --> 01:53:21,699
Everyone is here.
Aren't they cooked already?

812
01:53:22,185 --> 01:53:23,465
Whoops.

813
01:53:25,631 --> 01:53:28,531
Brothers! Bring those meats.

814
01:53:30,842 --> 01:53:36,522
- Ayaz Alp is hungry.
- Or Ayaz Alp will eat us all!

815
01:53:39,603 --> 01:53:42,543
Bamsı Bey! They're making fun of me!

816
01:53:46,559 --> 01:53:47,999
In the name of Allah!

817
01:53:50,782 --> 01:53:54,782
My valiants!

818
01:53:55,802 --> 01:53:59,072
Nine types of foods are
eaten at ceremonies.

819
01:53:59,419 --> 01:54:02,529
Red deers, lambs, birds...

820
01:54:03,642 --> 01:54:11,182
And if your Alp friend is with you,
you'd eat a rock for bread!

821
01:54:12,104 --> 01:54:13,564
Bamsı Bey is on fire!

822
01:54:17,792 --> 01:54:21,232
The ground cracks but
the Bey's commands keep coming...

823
01:54:22,516 --> 01:54:25,806
... the sweats are wiped
but the work doesn't end...

824
01:54:26,090 --> 01:54:29,780
... a feast is given
but the food doesn't end.

825
01:54:31,175 --> 01:54:35,175
As long as you're with a friend,
poison is honey for you!

826
01:54:41,467 --> 01:54:45,027
We shall give food to the poor,
a blanket to the cold!

827
01:54:45,166 --> 01:54:49,166
From now on, we shall burn
with the love of holy war!

828
01:54:50,095 --> 01:54:54,095
This is a feast! Eat as you like!
But...

829
01:54:54,394 --> 01:54:59,754
... but commemorate
the Prophet Mohammad!

830
01:55:01,658 --> 01:55:02,438
Now...

831
01:55:03,617 --> 01:55:06,547
Let the tents be tents and let
their lineage grow.

832
01:55:06,805 --> 01:55:08,765
Let the feast begin.

833
01:55:09,895 --> 01:55:15,085
Come on. Where is our poet? He...

834
01:55:15,480 --> 01:55:17,910
He understands us...

835
01:55:19,417 --> 01:55:22,357
He is famous for
his qopuz. (a Turkish instrument)

836
01:55:23,470 --> 01:55:26,680
Hey...

837
01:55:27,364 --> 01:55:31,064
This is the feast of Osman Bey!

838
01:55:31,306 --> 01:55:35,376
Hey! Mashaallah!

839
01:55:35,436 --> 01:55:37,556
Thank you, Bamsı Bey.

840
01:55:41,457 --> 01:55:43,767
Long live my Bey!

841
01:55:44,024 --> 01:55:47,254
- Long live!
- Thanks, Bamsı Bey...

842
01:55:47,441 --> 01:55:50,791
Thanks. Mashaallah.

843
01:56:01,893 --> 01:56:03,423
My father...

844
01:56:04,512 --> 01:56:06,492
See...

845
01:56:09,424 --> 01:56:13,184
Your grandchild Osman grew up and...

846
01:56:13,432 --> 01:56:15,772
...married.

847
01:56:16,979 --> 01:56:18,589
He started a family.

848
01:56:21,646 --> 01:56:23,766
I'm old, father.

849
01:56:24,571 --> 01:56:28,571
I wanted to be a son worthy of you...

850
01:56:29,535 --> 01:56:31,915
I tried during my whole life.

851
01:56:34,039 --> 01:56:36,529
But I couldn't.

852
01:56:39,086 --> 01:56:41,896
But I was unaware, father.

853
01:56:42,693 --> 01:56:45,663
It seems that I was blind...

854
01:56:46,206 --> 01:56:48,206
...and deaf.

855
01:56:50,623 --> 01:56:53,503
Ah...

856
01:56:56,515 --> 01:56:59,125
I'm old like you.

857
01:57:00,029 --> 01:57:02,559
However, I couldn't grow up like you.

858
01:57:04,138 --> 01:57:07,468
I even betrayed my own life.

859
01:57:09,464 --> 01:57:13,464
I betrayed myself and you...

860
01:57:13,996 --> 01:57:19,016
...and your tent.
Forgive me.

861
01:57:19,422 --> 01:57:21,282
Forgive me.

862
01:57:26,924 --> 01:57:29,494
I wish you were here...

863
01:57:29,729 --> 01:57:31,309
My mother...

864
01:57:32,272 --> 01:57:33,772
My father...

865
01:57:35,230 --> 01:57:36,940
My Batur..

866
01:57:39,250 --> 01:57:41,560
I wish you were with me.

867
01:57:42,436 --> 01:57:44,396
I wish you hugged me.

868
01:57:45,785 --> 01:57:48,515
You'd be a remedy to my wrongs and...

869
01:57:48,666 --> 01:57:51,426
...my heart.

870
01:57:53,598 --> 01:57:56,018
I wish I didn't do any of these.

871
01:57:57,845 --> 01:58:00,165
I wish we were together...

872
01:58:00,468 --> 01:58:02,298
...in this tent.

873
01:58:10,218 --> 01:58:14,218
The poet always says the truth.

874
01:58:15,191 --> 01:58:19,191
From now on, neither our azans
nor our poets...

875
01:58:19,670 --> 01:58:23,340
...will ever shut.

876
01:58:24,499 --> 01:58:26,069
Bard! (poet)

877
01:58:26,457 --> 01:58:29,627
Horse's foot is like crowbar and bard's
mouth is strong.

878
01:58:29,687 --> 01:58:33,687
- Strike the dombra's cord! ( a Turkish instrument)
- Thanks.

879
01:59:04,886 --> 01:59:08,506
When he became twenty...

880
01:59:09,339 --> 01:59:12,529
He dreamt something holy...

881
01:59:13,631 --> 01:59:17,161
He is the nightmare...

882
01:59:17,834 --> 01:59:21,224
...of the bad people, Osman Bey!

883
01:59:22,223 --> 01:59:25,683
He is so strong...

884
01:59:26,651 --> 01:59:29,991
...down with unbelievers!

885
01:59:31,006 --> 01:59:34,166
Ertuğrul Ghazi's valiant...

886
01:59:35,411 --> 01:59:39,411
Osman Bey is valiant...

887
01:59:44,005 --> 01:59:48,005
He is from an ancient family...

888
01:59:50,709 --> 01:59:54,709
The sky refers to him...

889
01:59:55,413 --> 01:59:58,513
He punished the cruels.

890
01:59:59,432 --> 02:00:02,542
Like a dark wolf, Osman Bey.

891
02:00:03,903 --> 02:00:07,453
He punished the cruels.

892
02:00:08,148 --> 02:00:11,908
Like a dark wolf, Osman Bey.

893
02:00:21,474 --> 02:00:24,554
With strong weapons...

894
02:00:25,638 --> 02:00:29,218
And hard equipments...

895
02:00:29,973 --> 02:00:33,593
...with valiant Alps...

896
02:00:34,279 --> 02:00:37,509
Osman Bey wrote history.

897
02:00:38,707 --> 02:00:42,227
While the oppressed people
are suffering...

898
02:00:43,094 --> 02:00:46,564
The earth calls for you...

899
02:00:47,477 --> 02:00:51,237
A state has been founded...

900
02:00:51,762 --> 02:00:55,422
Like sky, like Osman Bey.

901
02:01:00,614 --> 02:01:03,694
He became a nightmare for devils...

902
02:01:07,083 --> 02:01:10,583
The sky calls for him...

903
02:01:11,680 --> 02:01:15,000
He punished the cruels...

904
02:01:15,694 --> 02:01:19,424
Like a dark wolf, Osman Bey.

905
02:01:20,341 --> 02:01:23,221
He punished the cruels...

906
02:01:24,477 --> 02:01:27,557
Like a dark wolf, Osman Bey.

907
02:01:42,047 --> 02:01:44,037
Mashaallah!

908
02:01:44,568 --> 02:01:46,118
Thanks.

909
02:01:51,399 --> 02:01:52,349
My Sheikh...

910
02:01:53,020 --> 02:01:56,020
You brought good to our table.

911
02:01:56,474 --> 02:01:59,844
Pray for us, Inshallah.

912
02:02:00,045 --> 02:02:03,635
Don't leave us without your prayers.

913
02:02:15,965 --> 02:02:19,965
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(In the name of Allah, Most Gracious, Most Merciful)

914
02:02:20,649 --> 02:02:25,089
Thank Allah for creating us as a Muslim.

915
02:02:25,148 --> 02:02:26,798
Amin.

916
02:02:27,431 --> 02:02:29,091
My Allah...

917
02:02:30,011 --> 02:02:34,011
You're our intention and wish.

918
02:02:34,153 --> 02:02:38,973
- Don't let people insult us.
- Amin.

919
02:02:39,083 --> 02:02:43,083
- Keep our effort and love alive.
- Amin.

920
02:02:43,828 --> 02:02:45,898
My Allah...

921
02:02:45,978 --> 02:02:48,748
Our matter is the land...

922
02:02:48,805 --> 02:02:52,395
...and our fight is for Islam.

923
02:02:52,506 --> 02:02:55,256
Make our lands lively...

924
02:02:55,455 --> 02:02:59,455
- and make our people happy.
- Amin.

925
02:02:59,775 --> 02:03:01,225
My Allah...

926
02:03:01,517 --> 02:03:05,747
...make our valiant soldiers'
hearts open...

927
02:03:06,477 --> 02:03:09,757
- and good.
- Amin.

928
02:03:10,473 --> 02:03:15,583
Fulfill their hears with
belief and sacrament.

929
02:03:15,583 --> 02:03:16,923
Amin.

930
02:03:17,503 --> 02:03:20,273
Adorn their life with holy wars..

931
02:03:20,335 --> 02:03:25,105
...make their death with Shahada.

932
02:03:25,282 --> 02:03:26,752
Amin.

933
02:03:27,175 --> 02:03:29,085
My Allah...

934
02:03:30,034 --> 02:03:33,294
Don't make our valiant soldiers'...

935
02:03:33,470 --> 02:03:36,800
- life hard.
- Amin.

936
02:03:37,060 --> 02:03:40,070
Make us stand against cruel...

937
02:03:40,373 --> 02:03:44,373
...and make us merciful towards
good people.

938
02:03:45,255 --> 02:03:48,045
Make us so fair that...

939
02:03:48,249 --> 02:03:52,249
- we can be reliable.
- Amin.

940
02:03:52,303 --> 02:03:55,313
Make us so kind that...

941
02:03:55,336 --> 02:03:59,096
- we can be home to good people.
- Amin.

942
02:03:59,974 --> 02:04:03,614
Make us so erudite that...

943
02:04:03,924 --> 02:04:07,604
- we can be the mind of believers.
- Amin.

944
02:04:08,019 --> 02:04:11,449
Make us so big that...

945
02:04:12,256 --> 02:04:17,126
- we can be the nightmares of bad people.
- Amin.

946
02:04:18,716 --> 02:04:20,366
Al Fatihah.

947
02:04:54,100 --> 02:04:55,400
Daughter.

948
02:04:55,961 --> 02:04:57,921
The feast has begun, father.

949
02:04:58,390 --> 02:05:00,720
Yes, it has.

950
02:05:00,789 --> 02:05:04,969
Osman Bey is doing what he wants.
Let's go.

951
02:05:10,127 --> 02:05:13,347
Okay, daughter. Let's go.

952
02:05:14,113 --> 02:05:17,993
The feast has begun.
They're waiting for us.

953
02:05:18,855 --> 02:05:22,055
Come on, daughter.

954
02:05:23,618 --> 02:05:24,398
Come on.

955
02:06:46,648 --> 02:06:47,528
Uncle...

956
02:06:50,096 --> 02:06:51,806
Welcome.

957
02:06:52,706 --> 02:06:55,036
Thanks.

958
02:07:07,193 --> 02:07:08,453
My uncle...

959
02:07:11,128 --> 02:07:13,048
...is my guest tonight.

960
02:07:14,273 --> 02:07:16,663
In this feast...

961
02:07:18,601 --> 02:07:21,111
...we unite.

962
02:07:21,419 --> 02:07:22,639
Amin.

963
02:07:41,700 --> 02:07:43,770
Dündar Bey...

964
02:07:44,040 --> 02:07:45,920
Here you go.

965
02:08:07,282 --> 02:08:09,832
My Osman Bey is so respectful.

966
02:08:10,921 --> 02:08:14,241
Although his uncle has done bad, he
is good to him.

967
02:08:18,121 --> 02:08:20,641
It's not easy to be Osman Bey.

968
02:08:21,895 --> 02:08:25,025
Your heart must be wide like...

969
02:08:25,734 --> 02:08:28,024
...your anger.

970
02:08:37,117 --> 02:08:39,157
The meal is coming.

971
02:08:39,182 --> 02:08:41,882
Yes...

972
02:09:04,191 --> 02:09:06,641
What's it, Zöhre? You're anxious.

973
02:09:06,718 --> 02:09:09,918
No, I'm not.

974
02:09:10,456 --> 02:09:12,216
Why are you saying that?

975
02:10:00,370 --> 02:10:04,370
Enjoy your meal.
Come on.

976
02:10:40,593 --> 02:10:42,393
Mother, what did you do?

977
02:10:42,634 --> 02:10:46,104
Come on, let's clean it.

978
02:10:50,559 --> 02:10:51,939
Come on.

979
02:10:54,314 --> 02:10:55,884
Dündar Bey...

980
02:10:56,708 --> 02:10:59,418
...it's dark.
Come with us.

981
02:11:03,393 --> 02:11:06,793
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

982
02:11:08,737 --> 02:11:09,937
Stop!

983
02:11:23,495 --> 02:11:24,765
Don't...

984
02:11:25,082 --> 02:11:26,252
eat...

985
02:11:26,363 --> 02:11:27,633
...the food!

986
02:11:42,599 --> 02:11:44,169
What happened?

987
02:11:47,741 --> 02:11:49,601
This traitor...

988
02:11:50,368 --> 02:11:52,798
...poisoned the food.

989
02:11:53,002 --> 02:11:54,052
What?

990
02:11:57,991 --> 02:11:59,541
What are you saying?

991
02:12:10,927 --> 02:12:12,727
She's lying.

992
02:12:15,572 --> 02:12:17,922
If you say so...

993
02:12:24,859 --> 02:12:26,719
...eat it then.

994
02:13:15,599 --> 02:13:20,949
If someone is trying to
kill us, I kill that person.

995
02:13:21,873 --> 02:13:23,943
What are you doing, Hazal Hatun?

996
02:13:23,997 --> 02:13:25,767
We didn't even ask her!

997
02:13:26,350 --> 02:13:30,680
Hazal Hatun doesn't do anything
without proof, Gündüz Bey.

998
02:13:45,451 --> 02:13:48,951
- What are you doing?!
- Your lifes...

999
02:13:49,073 --> 02:13:52,263
are my wedding gift for you, Osman.

1000
02:13:54,813 --> 02:13:56,003
Now...

1001
02:13:56,782 --> 02:14:00,562
If you want to taste
the food, you can do it!

1002
02:14:00,960 --> 02:14:04,960
If you don't want to see how you die...

1003
02:14:05,017 --> 02:14:07,317
then don't.

1004
02:14:07,683 --> 02:14:11,483
There are lots of Beys here!
Why don't you tell us?

1005
02:14:12,677 --> 02:14:16,677
I do my job myself, Osman.

1006
02:14:19,447 --> 02:14:25,167
From now on, all of you owe me a life.